      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Petitioner Robyn Morgan worked as an hourly employee at a Taco Bell franchise owned by respondent Sundance. When applying for the job, Morgan signed an agreement to arbitrate any employment dispute."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2021-21-328",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5f9681d83b18ec27196b249b714269cded64cf31c4159df0d45a5463ed299cb1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5f9681d83b18-0000-0008",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Judge Colloton dissented. He argued that Sundance had \u201cled Morgan to waste time and money\u201d opposing the motion to dismiss and \u201cengaging in a fruitless mediation.\u201d"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-21-328",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5f9681d83b18ec27196b249b714269cded64cf31c4159df0d45a5463ed299cb1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5f9681d83b18-0000-0007",
      "kind": "holding",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Our sole holding today is that it may not make up a new procedural rule based on the FAA's \u201cpolicy favoring arbitration.\u201d"
    }
